---
title: "Chickpea and Leek Soup"
servings: 5
yield_verified: true
planner_ready: true
source: "https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/jamie-oliver/chickpea-and-leek-soup-recipe-1911871"
repository: "https://github.com/nicholaswilde/recipes/blob/main/cook/soups-and-stews/Chickpea%20and%20Leek%20Soup.cook"
author: "Jamie Oliver"
site: "GitHub · nicholaswilde/recipes"
tags: ["approachable"]
license: "Apache-2.0"
---
Drain and rinse the @canned chickpeas{1.667%cans}. Place the whole peeled
@medium potato{0.833} in a #pot, cover with @water, and simmer until soft.

In a separate thick-bottomed #pan, warm the @olive oil{0.833%Tbsp}
 and @butter{0.833%knob}. Add the sliced @medium leeks{4.167} and sliced
@garlic cloves{1.667} with a good pinch of @salt. Sweat them gently over low
heat until they are tender and sweet (do not brown them).

Drain the cooked chickpeas and potato. Add them to the pan with the leeks and
cook for ~{1%minute} to combine the flavors.

Add about two-thirds of the @chicken or vegetable stock{2 1/2%c} to the pan.
Bring to a simmer and let it cook for about ~{15%minutes}.

Puree exactly half of the mixture in a #food processor{} or with an
#immersion blender{}, leaving the other half chunky.

Stir the pureed half back into the pot. Add as much of the remaining
stock as needed to reach your preferred consistency. Season with @salt
and @freshly ground black pepper{} to taste. Stir in most of the grated
@Parmesan cheese{1/2%cup} to round off the flavors.

Ladle into #bowls. Finish with a generous drizzle of @extra-virgin olive oil{},
a fresh grinding of black pepper, and the remaining Parmesan cheese.
